so --all would walk one commit per ticket event — the wrong history, and an unbounded amount of it.'","docs/concurrency.md, docs/config.md, docs/adr/0031: the tickets branch is a real branch in the same repo carrying committed event blobs"],"finding":"Design step 1 specifies scanning with `git log --all` ('a strict superset of HEAD'), but rebar's default store layout keeps the ticket event log on a co-located `tickets` branch of the SAME repository, so `--all` walks one commit per ticket EVENT — the wrong, unbounded history — and worse, a `caused_by` target id that happens to appear in a ticket-event commit subject/trailer on the tickets branch would spuriously satisfy the 'shipped a commit' guard, a false-positive that lets a genuinely commit-less attribution through.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0352ca1babce4770","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design, step 1 ('Scan every ref, not just HEAD ... appends `--all`')","norm_id":"n3c70c7be821a482e","priority":0.9,"reason":"veto:plan-goal-satisfied","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A caused_by target id string incidentally present in a ticket-event commit subject on the co-located tickets branch → guard sees a 'referencing commit' that is not code → wrongly ALLOWS a commit-less attribution","A large store with many ticket events → --all scans an unbounded ticket-event history on every caused_by link, a performance regression"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Change Design step 1 so the opt-in flag scans HEAD plus the remote-tracking refs matching the checkout's current branch (e.g. an `upstream_branch_refs` helper: `symbolic-ref HEAD` → `for-each-ref refs/remotes/` filtered by that branch name), NOT `--all`; note explicitly that `--all` is rejected because rebar's default layout co-locates the ticket event log on a `tickets` branch, so `--all` walks the wrong history and can spuriously match a target id in a ticket-event commit.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_co